& [Implementation] is one thin executable adapter
  + crates/cantor_cli/Cargo.toml declares cantor-procedure-experiment
  + procedure_main.rs owns only transport forms, command dispatch, response and exit projection, and bounded I/O
  + schema delegates to provider_neutral_exchange_schema
  + run delegates to run_fake_controller_exchange and then requires verify_fake_controller_outcome before returning
  + verify delegates independently to verify_fake_controller_outcome and returns four exact bindings
  + no cantor_core semantic implementation changed

& [MachineBoundary] is stable
  + schema, run, and verify are the only commands
  + run and verify consume strict JSON through stdin or one --input path
  + ingress is empty-refusing and limited to 16777216 bytes
  + stdout is one newline-terminated JSON response
  + statuses map to exit codes success 0, invalid_input 2, refused 3, verification_failure 4, and internal_fault 5
  + adapter messages are limited to 1024 Unicode scalar values

& [Safety] is retained
  + all identities, hashes, procedures, lanes, policies, and outcomes are supplied explicitly
  + the adapter repairs or mints none of them
  + verified refusal remains a first-class outcome with exit 3
  + every response states zero model or provider calls, zero external semantic effects, and no production qualification

